{{!-- A titled group of move rows. Params: title, note, moves, categoryKey, allowAdditional,
      alwaysShowResource, and `unacquirable`.

      `disclosure` collapses every row in the group to a single line — see move-item.hbs.

      `unacquirable` drops the acquisition checkbox. The tick records that a CHARACTER has taken a
      move, so it only means something where there was a choice: a steading has all six of its
      homefront moves and all four Seasons Change moves from the day it exists, and a box that can
      never be unticked asserts a state that does not exist — while costing a column of width in a
      220px rail. Opt-in, so every group that does have something to acquire is unaffected. --}}
<div class="stonetop-move-group">
	{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=title note=note}}
	<ol class="items-list">
	{{#each moves}}
		{{> "stonetop.move-row" showCheck=(not ../unacquirable) categoryKey=../categoryKey allowAdditional=../allowAdditional alwaysShowResource=../alwaysShowResource disclosure=../disclosure}}
	{{/each}}
	</ol>
</div>
